  {
    "op": "add-textbox",
    "slide": "SLIDE_10",
    "text": "Data Model & Integrity Invariants",
    "x": 395,
    "y": 92,
    "width": 275,
    "height": 24,
    "font_size": 13,
    "bold": true,
    "color": "#0F172A",
    "font_family": "Roboto"
  },
  {
    "op": "add-textbox",
    "slide": "SLIDE_10",
    "text": "\u2022 Core Entities:\n  - `patients`: Demographics, language preference, contact.\n  - `doctors`: Specialty, license, status, consultation fee.\n  - `schedules`: Weekly recurring shifts and exception rules.\n  - `appointments`: Booking status, time range, cancellation reason.\n  - `support_tickets`: Issue tracking, urgency, resolution status.\n  - `audit_logs`: Immutable ledger of all data mutations.\n\n\u2022 Concurrency & Consistency:\n  - PostgreSQL exclusion constraints prevent overlapping slots.\n  - Optimistic concurrency control (version checks) on updates.\n  - UTC timestamps used uniformly across all services.",
    "x": 395,
    "y": 118,
    "width": 275,
    "height": 260,
    "font_size": 9.8,
    "color": "#334155",
    "font_family": "Roboto",
    "line_spacing": 140
  },
  {
    "op": "set-notes",
    "slide": "SLIDE_10",
    "text": "The ERD illustrates our relational data model in PostgreSQL. Database-level exclusion constraints guarantee that no double bookings can occur even under high concurrency."
  },
